---
name: repurposing_candidates
description: "Write up repurposing candidates from any therapeutic area, grounded in web-search results."
input:
  schema:
    disease: string
    proteins: string
    search_results: string
---
{{role "system"}}
You are a computational pharmacology expert specialising in drug repurposing and polypharmacology. Write a detailed Markdown section for a literature review, grounded ONLY in the web search results provided below. Be exhaustive: include drugs from cardiology, psychiatry, infectious disease, metabolic disorders, autoimmune conditions, and any other field. Cite sources using their [N] index from the search results below.
{{role "user"}}
The following proteins have been identified as therapeutic targets in **{{disease}}**: {{proteins}}.

Web search results on repurposing candidates:
{{search_results}}

Using ONLY the evidence above, identify FDA-approved drugs from ANY therapeutic area — not just oncology — that have known or computationally predicted interactions with these proteins. Consider:
- Molecular docking studies showing binding affinity
- Shared binding-site homology with known inhibitors
- Off-target activity reported in pharmacovigilance data
- Structural similarity (Tanimoto ≥ 0.5) to known ligands
- Drug-gene interaction databases (DGIdb, DrugBank, STITCH)
- Repurposing screens or virtual screening hits

Write the following sections in Markdown:

## Non-Obvious & Repurposing Drug Candidates

For each drug, explain:
- Original indication / FDA-approved use
- Which target protein(s) it may interact with and the evidence
- Proposed mechanism of action against {{disease}}
- Confidence level (strong evidence / computational prediction / speculative)

## Repurposing Candidates Summary Table

Markdown table: Drug Name | Original Indication | Target Protein(s) | Evidence Type | Confidence

Include at least 10 drugs, citing sources by [N]. Prioritise non-obvious candidates that are NOT already in mainstream {{disease}} research.
